# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's WP4 (MLP gate/up) card-M jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the card is
# resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the read rules and the decision rule.
# ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag the window's B0 builds (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env); the harness mounts this checkout's scripts, so the
# image only supplies ttnn. The cardm step runs card M alone (C2_CARDS=pair: cardm is a pair-shaped step) and never resets it; production is down for the window.
# C5 (WP4, after C1 and C3: WHY the gate streams at about half the down's rate, 240 GB/s of 512 against 381, and whether a reader change could move it). Three diagnostics in one job:
#   sweep   the gate and up shapes with bfloat8_b weights (gate_bf8, up_bf8: same tile count, twice the bytes): if they run at the bf4 shapes' TIME the limit is per tile (requests),
#           if at twice the time it is per byte; and `MLP_GATEUP epilogue` prints the SiLU epilogue the C1 rows imply (about 2.3 us per output column per core).
#   probe   the read-bandwidth probe: one data-movement kernel, no compute, that reads the whole weight (bfloat4_b and bfloat8_b at the gate shape, bfloat8_b at the down shape)
#           one tile page per request (the stock matmul reader's pattern) and in bank-contiguous multi-tile requests (the tiles (k, c), (k, c + 8), (k, c + 16) ... of a tile row
#           are adjacent pages of ONE DRAM bank in an interleaved tensor), with a copy-back correctness launch per point. READ: `MLP_GATEUP probe verdict`: READ-GRANULARITY
#           (bank-contiguous reads at least 1.25 times the stock pattern: build the bank-strided reader for the fused op), MARGINAL, NO-EFFECT.
#   split   the SiLU taken out of the gate matmul: A float32 gate, silu, typecast, multiply; B float32 gate and the multiply taking the SiLU as its input activation; C the same with a
#           bfloat16 gate (the control that must differ). READ: exact or not, and the delta in microseconds a layer.
# Applies nothing. Duration (estimate): 40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/mlp_gateup/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--shapes gate_bf8,up_bf8 --arms sweep,probe,split
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
